+  <div className="an-card"><h3>Integration contract with fastapispark</h3><pre>Lesson + fixture version + supported syntax{'\n'}  - compile source using POST /v1/spark/compile{'\n'}  - reject unsupported operations or compiler warnings{'\n'}  - validate against this lesson, server-side as well as client-side{'\n'}  - execute only the lesson fixture using POST /v1/spark/execute{'\n'}  - check all result rows, not only the displayed preview{'\n'}  - store the attempt separately from layout/source revisions</pre><p>{l.truth}</p><p>Current helper code only validates a compile-response envelope and prepares a bounded request. It neither makes a network request nor certifies the service as safe for arbitrary input. Server-side argument validation, version negotiation, full-result grading, authentication and conformance tests remain integration gates.</p></div></section>;
