+# UI M1 continuation handoff
+
+## Start here
+
+Continue `julian-passebecq/ducklabms_code`, branch `codex/real-spark-proxy-1`, PR #5.
+The source base is `abb0345a78836508f6024d79710a46973cbed9d6`; the preceding
+functional baseline is `5ace7654baad1bc2d2dd1254efa5abd2a55cbb3e`.
+Read architecture/00_START_HERE.md and existing contracts before editing.
+
+The user prioritizes a genuinely usable local interface before Spark, Oracle,
+dbt and cloud work: a Fabric-style notebook, movable lakehouse/notebook explorer,
+free coding canvas and integrated interview arena. This is one app.
+
+This pass is an implementation candidate, NOT a new released version. Full source
+assembly and production React/Vite/backend QA are deferred. See the update
+package's QA_STATUS.md and evidence. Never reuse the earlier baseline CI results
+as evidence for these new files.
+
+## Implemented integration
+
+NotebookDesktop consumes RootNotebook, Asset[], existing exercise metadata,
+renderBlock, the existing NotebookCanvas and existing save/run/submit callbacks.
+No source/runtime/catalog is copied into another product.
+
+The Notebook mode renders semanticBlocks in the order of the canonical notebook
+view. Canvas passes through the existing grid renderer and its layout changes.
+Arena selects the actual exercise answer and linked output cells and renders
+existing problem/help/evidence callbacks. Moving panels never changes semantic
+order. Run and Submit remain different backend operations.
+
+`preferredView?: string` is optional RootNotebook metadata, validated by
+normalizePreferredView during restore. Absence preserves the old object shape.
+UI mode, legacy tabs and presentation controls update it. Load/reopen uses it
+only after restore validation. Panel geometry is separate, validated browser-local
+state, keyed by workspace ID and notebook ID. It is not canonical notebook code.
+
+The editor replacement preserves the original Monaco adapter with a guarded
+plain-editor fallback. The keyboard helpers are pure and tested. Catalog preview
+SQL quotes schema/table segments and inserts a cell without execution.
+
+## Preview is explicit, not a backend fallback
+
+main.tsx opens UiPreview only for `?preview=1`. The fixture host reuses the new
+NotebookDesktop. Run and Submit stay disabled; example tables are labelled.
+It uses RootNotebook's shape and source keys but its exercise IDs are not installed
+backend packs. The standalone compiled harness uses offline React 16 bundles;
+the real application keeps its existing dependencies. Production must not use
+the fixture canvas adapter in place of the original NotebookCanvas.
+
+## Release work remaining
+
+Run full TypeScript/Vite validation before extending this candidate. Test it on
+the full pinned source; the editing session could only fetch individual baseline
+files, not the complete source or dependencies. Run the new UI-only Playwright
+configuration first, then the connected save/reopen test and existing V1 smoke.
+Qualify Monaco, live original grid layout, actual catalog/SQL, Python opt-in,
+Run/Submit evidence, old notebook imports and narrow screens. Legacy broad browser
+selectors may need updates, but do not weaken their behavioral assertions.
+
+Do not hide API errors by silently selecting fixtures. Keep unavailable execution
+unavailable. Do not add another notebook model, grader, dataset store or cloud
+requirement to solve an interface problem.
+
+Cloudflare config is static assets plus explicit 503 for /api, not a runtime
+migration. No provider auth/proxy/deployment is implemented. Revisit this only
+after the local UI milestone passes real-app QA.
